<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
 <head>
  <title>CSS Test: Background with image, repeat-x, and position bottom</title>
  <link rel="author" title="Microsoft" href="http://www.microsoft.com/" />
  <link rel="help" href="http://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/colors.html#propdef-background" />
  <link rel="match" href="background-position-bottom-001-ref.xht" />
  <meta name="flags" content="image" />
  <meta name="assert" content="Background with (color image repeat-x bottom) sets the background to the color specified, with the image overlaid across the x-axis at the bottom." />
  <style type="text/css">
  div {
    background: green url("support/blue15x15.png") bottom repeat-x;
    height: 200px;
    width: 200px;
  }
  </style>
 </head>
 <body>
  <p>Test passes if there is a green rectangle on top of a blue stripe.</p>
  <div></div>
 </body>
</html>